.TH IMUD\-INFLUXDB 8 "2026-09-06" "imud 1.10.1" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-influxdb \- bridge imud's binary stream to InfluxDB line protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-influxdb
\&[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\&[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-influxdb
connects to the local AF_UNIX binary subscription stream published by
.BR imud (8)
and writes one InfluxDB
.I line-protocol
point per tick, for time-series storage and Grafana dashboards (fusion tuning,
sea-trial logging).  Two transports are supported:
.TP
.B udp
Fire-and-forget datagrams to InfluxDB 1.x's UDP listener or Telegraf's
.I socket_listener
(the usual path into InfluxDB 2.x/3.x).  Configure the listener precision as ns.
.TP
.B http
A plaintext HTTP POST per point to
.I /write
(1.x) or
.I /api/v2/write
(2.x), with an optional
.B Authorization: Token
header.  No TLS \(em front a cloud/TLS endpoint with a local proxy.
.PP
The bridge holds no hardware and is pure C (no external dependencies).  It reads
the stream socket named by its own
.B socket
key (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ),
so
.BR imud (8)
must have its
.B [stream]
output enabled, and it reconnects automatically if imud restarts.
.PP
Each point carries the measurement (default
.IR imud ),
a
.B source
tag, and fields: quaternion
.RB ( qw , qx , qy , qz ),
.BR roll / pitch / yaw ,
.BR heading ,
.BR heading_true / variation
(when declination is known),
.BR rate_of_turn ,
.B heave
with
.BR heave_rate " and " heave_valid
(when
.B publish_heave
is set), the gyro-bias diagnostics
.RB ( gbias_x/y/z ", " gbias_var_x/y/z )
and
.B quiescence
(always), the compass-health metrics
.RB ( mag_anomaly ", " mag_residual )
(always), the sea-state fields
.RB ( wave_height ", " wave_period ", " roll_period ", " roll_amplitude ", "\
 pitch_period ", " pitch_amplitude " with " wave_valid )
(always; 0.0 until settled),
.BR temp ,
and an integer
.BR seq ,
timestamped with the packet's wall-clock time in nanoseconds.  Angles are
degrees
.RB ( units " = " deg )
or radians
.RB ( units " = " rad );
the heave-rate, gyro-bias, quiescence, compass-health and sea-state
diagnostics are always SI (m/s, rad/s, (rad/s)\[u00B2], m, s, rad)
regardless of
.BR units .
.IP
InfluxDB bridge: reads imud's stream socket and writes InfluxDB
line\-protocol points over UDP (default) or HTTP.
Configured by [imud\-influxdb] in its own file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR PATH
Config file (default: \fI\,/etc/imud/imud\-influxdb.conf\/\fP)
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help and exit
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.  The rate, measurement, source tag, units, heave
inclusion, UDP destination, and log level are applied live; the transport and
HTTP target require a restart.  If the reload fails to parse, the running
configuration is kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read from
.I /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
(the
.B [imud-influxdb]
section); the keys are documented in
.BR imud-influxdb.conf (5).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
Default configuration file, installed mode 0640 owner
.I root:imud
because it can hold a plaintext InfluxDB API token.
A file that exists but cannot be read is fatal \(em the bridge refuses to start
rather than run on defaults.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run against a local InfluxDB 1.x UDP listener:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-influxdb --config /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable as a service (after enabling imud's
.B [stream]
output and at least one bridge output \(em
.B udp_enabled
and/or
.B http_enabled
\(em in
.IR imud-influxdb.conf ;
the daemon itself is enabled by default):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl enable --now imud-influxdb
.EE
.RE
